@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Public route: /restaurants works with NO token (Criterion 4 -> 200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/restaurants

###

### 2. Protected route: /orders fails with NO token (Criterion 4 -> 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders

###

### 3. Register a new user (Criterion 1 & 2 -> 201 Created, NO passwordHash/refreshHash in response)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "abdi.test@addiseats.et",
  "password": "StrongPassword123!"
}

###

### 4. Register duplicate email (Deliverable -> 409 Conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "abdi.test@addiseats.et",
  "password": "StrongPassword123!"
}

###

### 5a. Login with wrong password (Deliverable -> 401 "Invalid credentials")
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "abdi.test@addiseats.et",
  "password": "WrongPassword!"
}

###

### 5b. Login with non-existent email (Deliverable -> same 401 "Invalid credentials" message)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@addiseats.et",
  "password": "StrongPassword123!"
}

###

### 6. Login with valid credentials (captures accessToken & refreshToken; Criterion 2 -> no hashes)
# @name loginReq
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "abdi.test@addiseats.et",
  "password": "StrongPassword123!"
}

###

### 7. Protected route: GET /orders WITH valid Bearer token (Criterion 4 -> 200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{loginReq.response.body.accessToken}}

###

### 8. Protected route: GET /auth/me returns req.user (Deliverable -> 200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{loginReq.response.body.accessToken}}

###

### 9. Tampered JWT payload (modify one character in the middle segment -> Criterion 3 -> 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{loginReq.response.body.accessToken}}tampered

###

### 10. Refresh & rotate tokens (Criterion 1 -> 200 OK with new accessToken & refreshToken)
# @name refreshReq
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{loginReq.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}

###

### 11. Replay old rotated refreshToken (verifies rotation invalidated the old token -> 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{loginReq.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}

###

### 12. Call /auth/me with the NEW rotated accessToken (200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{refreshReq.response.body.accessToken}}